# Geʽez Abugida | Geminated/Composite Geʽez Syllables Rules
# [AUTHOR]: Carlos González Sanz
#
# [Main source]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geʽez_script#Unicode
#
# [NOTE]: All syllables contained in this file count as geminated consonant + vowel
# (or even composite consonants + vowel) pairs, at least according
# to their main Unicode aliases. Additionally, this file
# offers an alternative for entering certain Geʽez syllables
# if they become unavailable as base characters
# on any SMK-Ethiopic keyboard layout.
#
# [NOTE]: All syllable combinations in this file are formed by fusing the corresponding
# base consonant + vocalized አ (ʼÄlf). These base "vowels" are:
#   - አ (ʼÄlf + Ä [æ])      [U+12A0 | U12A0]
#   - ኡ (ʼÄlf + U [u])      [U+12A1 | U12A1]
#   - ኢ (ʼÄlf + I [i])      [U+12A2 | U12A2]
#   - ኣ (ʼÄlf + A [aː])     [U+12A3 | U12A3]
#   - ኤ (ʼÄlf + E [e])      [U+12A4 | U12A4]
#   - እ (ʼÄlf + Ə [ɨ])      [U+12A5 | U12A5]
#   - ኦ (ʼÄlf + O [o])      [U+12A6 | U12A6]
#   - ኧ (ʼÄlf + WA [ʷaː])   [U+12A7 | U12A7]
#   - ⶊ (ʼÄlf + OA [ɔ])     [U+2D8A | U2D8A]
#

